    "Deterministic evaluations"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "We want to optimize a target function $f: \\mathcal{X} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ under a budget $\\Lambda\\in \\mathbb{R_+}$. The evaluation of this target function is done through its fidelity approximations. ... A known cost function $\\lambda$ indicates the budget used at each evaluation for a given fidelity. ... We then define the simple regret of a policy $\\pi$ for $r_\\Lambda$ as $r_\\Lambda(\\pi) \\triangleq \\mathbb{E}[\\max_{x} f(x) - f(x_\\Lambda)]$"
  },
